  "query_preview": ".. (Sunday night through Friday) \nIssued at 751 AM EDT SAT AUG 15 2026\n\nA ripple moving through the mid-upper level flow to our north will \nsupport a weak cold front which is expected to approach us Sunday \nnight and move through on Monday or Monday evening. Deeper moisture \nshould return ahead of the front, with our PWs rising to around 2\" \nagain. With this, the potential for thunderstorms returns. Drier air \narriving behind the front will probably keep us mostly dry on \nTuesday. However, there is a shortwave trough showing up in some\nof the latest guidance and results in a bit of spotty precip. The\nNBM forecast is dry on Tuesday. However, if the shortwave and its\nprecip persist in later model runs, a low POP could end up in \nlater forecasts.\n\nThe next significant shot at precip arrives in the neighborhood of \nWednesday night and Thursday as an upper level impulse carves out an \neastern CONUS trough. This sends another cold front southeast, with \natmospheric moisture again increasing ahead of the front. Behind the \nfront, there could be some noticeable relief from the mugginess at \nthe end of the week.",
